-- title:
--   Literal discounted ruin-stopped original compensated jump bands converge in absolute L1(P) integral
-- statement:
--   Using original path jump NX and exact finite-band source representation, prove that the actual compensated stochastic integral ∫(Bn GW)dNX−∫∫(Bn GW)dν dclock tends to the centered L2(P) limit in the ordinary expectation of absolute difference. Original filtration and inclusive ruin stop/discount are preserved; source isometry remains explicit as Chat01 obligation. This is the source-exact L1 limit exchange for Chat06.
-- source:
--   Start with the canonically accepted absolute L1-error integral convergence for the Lp2 isometry approximants. The exact hSource gives a.e. equality with the literal original jump measure compensated expression; Lp.coeFn_sub lifts that equality to absolute errors. Bochner integral_congr_ae transports the convergence.

